Subject: [PATCH] settings: validate restored values before applying properties

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD persistent settings recovery]

Validate the entire restored object before setters can serialize partial data.
Convert size-limit rejection to the archive exception already handled by the
manager: log the affected object, remove the invalid archive and initialize
all properties on that object from defaults. D-Bus writes retain InvalidArgument.

--- a/settings_manager.hpp.mako
+++ b/settings_manager.hpp.mako
@@ -390,5 +390,16 @@
     }
 % endif
+    try
+    {
+% for p in props:
+        checkPersistentSettingSize(${p['prop']});
+% endfor
+    }
+    catch (const sdbusplus::xyz::openbmc_project::Common::Error::InvalidArgument&)
+    {
+        throw cereal::Exception("Persisted setting exceeds board size limits on ${object}");
+    }
+
 <% props = [] %>
 % for index, item in enumerate(settingsDict[object]):
   % for  prop, metaDict in item['Properties'].items():
